Z||000000||bHooper||11-05-2001||06:53 PM||||ok.. this auto tranny has been driving me mad.<P>i swapped the detent cable with the one from the Fiero Store, and fianlly have it adjusted to drop into 3rd gear (in other words shifting though all the gears).<P>however, it still seems to "slip" when i stand on the throttle sometimes.  it is also accompanied by a noise (cant describe it... it's not loud or distinct, but there).  so what is going on?  is it the torque convertor on it's way out?  <P>i've got some "tranny conditioner" stuff that i am planning on putting in the car.  will that help some?<P>thanks!<BR><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
