Z||000002||btoth||11-06-2001||06:50 PM||||Well, mine shifts nice and smooth (when warm) when accelerating like a normal person. When I floor it, it will go up to almost the red before shifting, there is a slight "slip" between shifts - it doesn't just go right to 2nd instantly, and it's kinda hard when it does.  Seems like most automatics that I've driven... even better than some new ones.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>0~40ish in 1st; 40ish~65ish in 2nd.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||11-06-2001||07:08 PM||||<A HREF="http://www.alldata.com/" TARGET=_blank>ALLDATA's</A> DIY service has at least a dozen TSB listed on transmission issues. The short answer is if it's not low fluid, the TV cable, or the governor it's an internal problem.<P>You might get really lucky and get some dirt that a cleaner/conditioner might remove but don't hold your breath...<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||11-06-2001||07:42 PM||||i thought i had the fluid levels right.  so b4 i put the conditioner in, i draind just a bit (with the vacuum brake bleeder).  it was kinda dark red (not the same color of the stuff i just put in), and then i added the conditioner, cranked the car and shifted through the gears as directed.<P>upon checking the fluid it was barely covering the tip of the dipstick, so i added another quart and shifted through the gears again.  the levels appear to be fine, now.<P>i haven't taken the car for a spin... will do that tomorrow nite.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
